<title>UK: HORSE RACING-CHELTENHAM FESTIVAL RESULTS.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-CHELTENHAM FESTIVAL RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>CHELTENHAM, England 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of grade</p>
<p>one feature races on Tuesday, the opening day of the Cheltenham</p>
<p>jump racing Festival:</p>
<p>Arkle Challenge Trophy steeplechase over two miles (3.2 kms)</p>
<p> 1. Or Royal    11-2 (ridden by Tony McCoy)</p>
<p> 2. Squire Silk 11-2 (Jamie Osborne)</p>
<p> 3. Celibate    13-2 (Jamie Railton)</p>
<p>Nine ran.</p>
<p>Mulligan, the 11-10 favourite, fell.</p>
<p>Distances: Half a length, six lengths.</p>
<p>Winner owned by David Johnson and trained by Martin Pipe in</p>
<p>England.</p>
<p>Value to winner: 53,762 pounds ($86,000).</p>
<p>Champion Hurdle run over two miles (3.2 kms)</p>
<p> 1. Make A Stand   7-1 (Tony McCoy)</p>
<p>2. Theatreworld  33-1 (Norman Williamson)</p>
<p>3. Space Trucker  9-2 (John Shortt)</p>
<p>17 ran. Large Action ,  7-2 favourite, pulled up.</p>
<p>Distances: Five lengths, three-quarters of a length.</p>
<p>Winner owned by Peter Deal and trained by Martin Pipe in</p>
<p>England.</p>
<p>Value to winner: 124,138 pounds ($198,620)</p>
</text>
